# ============================================================
# cloud-stack environment (used by docker-compose.yaml)
#
# Local:     cp .env.example .env  and fill in the values
# Portainer: add the same variables under
#            Stacks -> cloud-stack -> Environment variables
#            (or use "Load variables from .env file")
#
# Never commit the real .env file.
# Keep comments on their own lines: some loaders do not strip
# inline comments and would put them inside the value.
# Generate secrets with:  openssl rand -hex 32
#
# This stack has two variables, both for MinIO.
# ============================================================

# --- MinIO ---
# Root credentials for the S3 store. Equivalent to full
# administrative control, so give applications their own service
# account rather than these.
#
# These are applied when minio_data is first initialised.
# Changing them here afterwards has no effect; change them in
# the console under Configuration -> Identity & Access ->
# Root Credentials.
MINIO_ROOT_USER=change-me
# openssl rand -hex 32
MINIO_ROOT_PASSWORD=change-me